---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const catalog = await import('../../public/dashboard-data/ai-learning-catalog.json');
const concepts = catalog.default.concepts;
const guides = catalog.default.guides;
const stackRadar = catalog.default.stack_radar;

const conceptLinks = [
  { label: 'AI agents', id: 'agent' },
  { label: 'LLMs', id: 'llm' },
  { label: 'VLMs', id: 'vlm' },
  { label: 'Tool calling', id: 'tool-calling' },
  { label: 'LangChain', id: 'langchain' },
  { label: 'RAG', id: 'rag' },
  { label: 'RBAC', id: 'rbac' },
  { label: 'Audit logs', id: 'audit-log' },
  { label: 'Observability', id: 'observability' },
  { label: 'AML', id: 'aml' },
  { label: 'False positives', id: 'false-positive' },
  { label: 'EVM', id: 'evm' },
  { label: 'Kubernetes', id: 'kubernetes' },
  { label: 'Docker', id: 'docker' },
];

const basicsRoute = [
  {
    label: 'Fintech rails',
    href: '/blog/fintech/',
    summary: 'Why finance keeps turning into software, and where the real risk moves.'
  },
  {
    label: 'Aave lending',
    href: '/blog/aave/',
    summary: 'Collateral, rates, and why on-chain credit behaves like a live risk machine.'
  },
  {
    label: 'Uniswap pools',
    href: '/blog/uniswap/',
    summary: 'The simple swap button, the pool underneath, and the risk liquidity carries.'
  },
  {
    label: 'DeFi basics',
    href: '/blog/defi/',
    summary: 'A first map for lending, borrowing, trading, and custody without the usual rails.'
  },
  {
    label: 'Zero-knowledge privacy',
    href: '/blog/zkp-explained/',
    summary: 'A privacy idea worth understanding before AI and finance get too close.'
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Knowledge Base" description="Plain-English concepts behind the Bionic Banker public work: AI agents, LLMs, VLMs, RAG, LangChain, RBAC, AML, observability, and deployment basics.">
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="page-label">Knowledge Base</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">Learn the terms behind the work.</h1>
    <p class="page-sub">Plain-English notes for the public pages. No hype. Just what each concept means, why it matters, and where it shows up.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="articles-wrap">
    <div class="article-card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
      <div class="article-tags">
        <span class="tag-pill tag-green">Start here</span>
      </div>
      <h3>The rule</h3>
      <p>The best way to learn AI is to build one small loop, make the output visible, and add a check so the system cannot only clap for itself.</p>
      <p>This page is the map behind the public pages. If a card says tool calling, RAG, RBAC, AML, false positive, or observability, this page explains the idea without making you read the whole archive.</p>
      <div class="concept-jump-list">
        {conceptLinks.map((item) => (
          <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>
        ))}
        <a href="/wallet-risk">Open Wallet Risk</a>
        <a href="/projects">Open systems</a>
        <a href="/reports">Reports</a>
        <a href="/gaps">Questions</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="route-rail" aria-label="Bionic Banker learning path">
      <div>
        <span class="section-label">Route</span>
        <h2>Follow the evidence workflow</h2>
        <p>Start with a question, learn the term, open the risk and evidence overview, then check the numbers. Each page is a different doorway into the same work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="route-links">
        <a href="/gaps">Questions</a>
        <a href="/learn">Knowledge Base</a>
        <a href="/risk-evidence-overview">Risk & Evidence Overview</a>
        <a href="/reports">Reports</a>
        <a href="/intelligence">Risk signals</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="basics-route" aria-label="Finance and AI basics route">
      <div class="basics-head">
        <span class="section-label">Basics</span>
        <h2>Start with the rails.</h2>
        <p>These are the plain notes I would hand someone before the work gets technical: money movement, pools, lending, privacy, and the risk that follows each layer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="basics-grid">
        {basicsRoute.map((item) => (
          <a class="basic-link-card" href={item.href}>
            <span>{item.label}</span>
            <p>{item.summary}</p>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="article-card" aria-label="How Bionic Banker explains hard concepts">
      <div class="article-tags">
        <span class="tag-pill tag-green">How to read this</span>
      </div>
      <h2>The explanation pattern</h2>
      <p>Every hard concept should become one normal reading path: name the thing, show what appears on screen, explain what is happening underneath, point to the record, then name the limit.</p>
      <p>A wallet row is a good example. The page shows a score and a note. Underneath, rules are checking patterns. The record shows which rule fired. The limit says the row is not a legal decision, not a KYC approval, and not permission to trade.</p>
      <p>That is the goal of this knowledge base. Not more jargon. Better handles for the same system.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="stack-radar-panel">
      <div class="section-label">Knowledge Map</div>
      <div class="radar-head">
        <div>
          <h2>What the work keeps returning to</h2>
          <p>AI work is not only prompting. It is retrieval, evals, traces, permission checks, deployment, and enough context that another person can follow the path.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/risk-evidence-overview">Open the Risk & Evidence Overview -></a>
      </div>
      <div class="radar-grid">
        {stackRadar.map((item, index) => (
          <article class="radar-card" id={item.id}>
            <div class="radar-index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <h3>{item.layer}</h3>
            <p><strong>Why it matters now:</strong> {item.why_2026_teams_care}</p>
            <p><strong>Learn here:</strong> {item.learn_here}</p>
            <p><strong>Question to ask:</strong> {item.reader_question}</p>
            <a href={item.linked_surface}>Follow this layer -></a>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-grid">
      {guides.map((guide) => (
        <article class="article-card animate-on-scroll">
          <div class="article-tags">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-green">Guide</span>
          </div>
          <h3>{guide.title}</h3>
          <ol class="tight-list">
            {guide.items.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </article>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section class="concept-grid">
      {concepts.map((concept) => {
        const subtitles = {
          'rag':          'Retrieval-Augmented Generation. An AI that looks things up before answering.',
          'rbac':         'Role-Based Access Control. Who can see what, and why it matters in finance.',
          'vlm':          'Vision Language Model. An AI that reads images and text together.',
          'langchain':    'A toolkit for connecting AI models to real data sources.',
          'aml':          'Anti-Money Laundering. The rules that flag suspicious financial patterns.',
          'false-positive': 'A flag that fires when it should not. The analyst still has to clear it.',
          'evm':          'Ethereum Virtual Machine. The engine that runs smart contracts on Ethereum.',
          'kubernetes':   'A system that keeps software services running reliably at scale.',
          'docker':       'A way to package software so it runs the same way on any machine.',
          'observability': 'The ability to see what is happening inside a system while it runs.',
          'audit-log':    'A time-stamped record of who did what. Common in finance and compliance.',
          'tool-calling': 'An AI that can run real functions, not just generate text.',
          'llm':          'Large Language Model. The kind of AI that reads and generates text.',
          'agent':        'An AI that takes actions in a loop, not just answers a single question.',
        };
        return (
        <article class="article-card animate-on-scroll concept-card" id={concept.id}>
          <div class="article-tags">
            <span class="tag-pill tag-green">Concept</span>
          </div>
          <h3>{concept.term}</h3>
          {subtitles[concept.id] && <p class="concept-subtitle">{subtitles[concept.id]}</p>}
          <p><strong>Meaning:</strong> {concept.plain_definition}</p>
          <p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> {concept.why_it_matters}</p>
          <p><strong>Shows up in:</strong> {concept.used_in.join(' / ')}</p>
          <div class="card-footer">
            <a class="read-more" href="/projects">Back to systems -></a>
            <a class="read-more" href="/reports">View report -></a>
            <a class="read-more" href="/gaps">View questions -></a>
          </div>
        </article>
        );
      })}
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .concept-jump-list {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      margin-top: 1.2rem;
    }

    .concept-jump-list a {
      border: 1px solid rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.35);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
      background: rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.08);
      min-height: 44px;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .guide-grid,
    .concept-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .route-rail {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(260px, 0.8fr);
      gap: 1rem;
      align-items: center;
      border: 1px solid rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.22);
      background: rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.055);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .route-rail h2 {
      margin: 0.2rem 0 0.45rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.3vw, 1.9rem);
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .route-rail p {
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .route-links {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.55rem;
      justify-content: flex-end;
    }

    .route-links a {
      border: 1px solid rgba(228, 228, 236, 0.14);
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--text);
      padding: 0.48rem 0.7rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      background: rgba(2, 2, 4, 0.35);
      min-height: 44px;
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
    }

    .basics-route {
      border: 1px solid rgba(228, 228, 236, 0.12);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.032);
      padding: 1.1rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .basics-head {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .basics-head h2 {
      margin: 0.2rem 0 0.45rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 2.1rem);
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .basics-head p {
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .basics-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(210px, 1fr));
      gap: 0.75rem;
    }

    .basic-link-card {
      min-height: 160px;
      border: 1px solid rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.22);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.055);
      color: var(--text);
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding: 1rem;
      text-decoration: none;
      touch-action: manipulation;
      transition: border-color 160ms ease, transform 160ms ease, background 160ms ease;
    }

    .basic-link-card:hover,
    .basic-link-card:focus-visible {
      border-color: rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.55);
      background: rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.09);
      transform: translateY(-2px);
    }

    .basic-link-card span {
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }

    .basic-link-card p {
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.55;
      margin: 1rem 0 0;
    }

    .tight-list {
      margin: 0;
      padding-left: 1.2rem;
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .concept-card {
      scroll-margin-top: 96px;
    }

    .concept-subtitle {
      color: var(--text-3);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      line-height: 1.45;
      margin: 0.1rem 0 0.5rem;
    }

    .stack-radar-panel {
      border: 1px solid rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.22);
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.35rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    }

    .radar-head {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      align-items: end;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .radar-head h2 {
      margin: 0.25rem 0 0.5rem;
      font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 2.2rem);
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .radar-head p {
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 760px;
    }

    .radar-head a,
    .radar-card a {
      color: #1fa068;
      text-decoration: none;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .radar-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
      gap: 0.85rem;
    }

    .radar-card {
      border: 1px solid rgba(228, 228, 236, 0.12);
      border-radius: 8px;
      background:
        linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(31, 160, 104, 0.08), transparent 42%),
        rgba(2, 2, 4, 0.46);
      padding: 1rem;
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .radar-index {
      color: #1fa068;
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    }

    .radar-card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      letter-spacing: 0;
    }

    .radar-card p {
      color: var(--text-2);
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .radar-head {
        align-items: flex-start;
        flex-direction: column;
      }

      .route-rail {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .route-links {
        justify-content: flex-start;
      }

      .basic-link-card {
        min-height: 132px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
